WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.550
Each period fills a shell; then the outer electrons start again at one.

2
00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:08.875
Lithium: period two starts with one outer electron.

3
00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:15.079
Across the period, one more each time, up to neon, with a full shell.

4
00:00:17.332 --> 00:00:21.982
Sodium starts a new shell and a new period, back to one outer electron.

5
00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:26.659
So the pattern repeats, and sodium behaves like lithium.
